  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "\"cry\" covers both producing tears and shouting. Many languages use two unrelated verbs for these; check which one a sentence means before translating.",
    "grammar": "\"cry\" has no object for tears in ordinary use: *she cried*, not a verb plus *tears* (*cry tears* is rare and literary).",
